    "text": "<p>A point source of light <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>, placed at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> infront of the centre of a plane mirror of width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, hangs vertically on a wall. A man walks infront of the mirror along a line parallel to the mirror at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;from it (see in the figure). The distance between the extreme points where he can see the image of the light source in the mirror is__<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0149_a6dfd7834208.png\" style=\"width: 269px; height: 143px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "150",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0149_96fcb8f82edb.png\" style=\"width: 306px; height: 239px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>60</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>180</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>so distance between extreme point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>"
  }
